{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aegis/1525396-mythological-realms-in-tc-aegis","id":1525396,"title":"Mythological Realms in TC Aegis","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aegis"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-11-13T01:12:43-08:00","id":1525396,"title":"Mythological Realms in TC Aegis","content":"<b>Do Hades - as realm - exists in Aegis? </b>Or Olympus - as realm? \ud83e\udd14 Even as some sort 's-f mamo jumbo'? <br /> <br /> Maybe as some 'Realm Between Dimension'?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-13T01:30:57-08:00","id":1525397,"title":"","content":"The possibility is there. Remember places like the underground lost land in Adventure 1e. Still I don't think it likely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-13T08:30:26-08:00","id":1525400,"title":"","content":"If they do, they're probably Strange Places. In particular, if you want to do a story like Orpheus in TC:Aegis, the Storyguide can certainly say that the protagonists find an entrance to the Underworld, which modern Talents would recognize as a dimensional gateway to a world that resembles Hades. <br /> <br /> But in the default setting? I'll be surprised if the developers ever give a green light to the notion that Hades <i>is</i> a thing in the TC:Aegis setting. Likewise with Olympus: while we have Olympians (i.e., \u201ceximorphs\u201d), the closest you're likely to get to Olympus is a base of operations on the physical Mount Olympus founded by TC:Aegis eximorphs. <i>Not </i>the home of the gods such as Zeus or Hera, unless you end up with Olympians styling themselves as Zeus or Hera. <br /> <br /> Remember, TC:Aegis isn't \u201cthe myths of ancient Greece are true\u201d; that's a Scion thing. TC:Aegis is \u201ca sufficiently advanced technology\u201d which, in many respects, is similar <i>enough</i> to aspects of ancient Greek mythology that they get mistaken for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-13T08:59:50-08:00","id":1525401,"title":"","content":"I would generally agree...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aegis/1525396-mythological-realms-in-tc-aegis?p=1525400#post1525400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But in the default setting? I'll be surprised if the developers ever give a green light to the notion that Hades <i>is</i> a thing in the TC:Aegis setting. Likewise with Olympus: while we have Olympians (i.e., \u201ceximorphs\u201d), the closest you're likely to get to Olympus is a base of operations on the physical Mount Olympus founded by TC:Aegis eximorphs. <i>Not </i>the home of the gods such as Zeus or Hera, unless you end up with Olympians styling themselves as Zeus or Hera.</div> </div> </div> </div>But in crowdfunding draft we have things like this...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TC Aegis Draft - Chapter 2, p. 26</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The founding members of the Order of Titans took upon themselves the pseudonyms of Uranus\u2019 forgotten children \u2014 Crius, Iapetus, Hyperion, Phoebe, and Tethys \u2014 and banded together with a singular goal: to restore the world to the way it was before enlightenment. Change swept in with the discovery of ambrosia. Calling themselves the \u201cPantheon,\u201d the five founding members and their followers have spread across the world, sowing discord upon the premise that \u201cWhat has happened once will happen again\u201d \u2014 meaning that just as Zeus overthrew Cronus, so, too will Zeus \u2014 or those Inspired individuals claiming his power \u2014 be overthrown. It\u2019s a matter of when, not if. These upheavals can end, so long as the Titans are the last ones standing atop the mountain.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this...<br /> [QUOTE = 'TC Aegis Draft - Chapter 2, p. 26'] The Order of the Titans is ruled by a council of five known as the Pantheon. Of these five, Crius is seen as the first among them as equals, followed then in order by Tethys, Iapetus, Phoebe, and Hyperion. They are, to a degree, the Titanic corollaries to the core Olympian gods \u2014 Zeus, Hades, Poseidon, Demeter,and Hera \u2014 and relish in acting in ways antithetical to their counterparts while maintaining a close enough similarity to confuse those less informed. From these five do all orders and endeavors come down, and very few question them on account that the killing of messengers is a common cause of death.\u200b\u200b[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> It's a bit fan interprataion, but I can see easily proper 'Theoi' Pantheon - with eximorphs calling themselves Zeus, Hades, Poseidon, Demeter and Hera - that once resided on Mount Olympus - or even Strange Place reflection of it, to plot taking control about whole Hellada.<br /> <br /> It's even interesting with Society of Lion taking whole 'physical' Mound Olympus under they care - they would need somekind of agreement with 'Theoi' over the same place. It's even more logical why Society of Lion do not want others to walk high into mountain top... \ud83d\ude08","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-28-2024, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}